This patch changes the whatis command '/' to use a menu,
and adds an option to perform a query on an inventory
item.


What do you want to look at:

a - something on the map
b - something you're carrying
c - something else


Options a and c correspond to the 'y' and 'n' options in
the query in the current vanilla, so no functionality is lost.
(a does the map lookup, b asks for user to type in the string)

The inventory item query will just get info for the item's
base type, eg. "dagger", or description if it's not identified.


